WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.919 --> 00:00:05.460
Death is a constant presence in Game of Thrones,
and the show made it very clear very early

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.180
on that it can come for even the most vital
characters.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.890
With the final season looming, no one is safe,
and the battlefields of Westeros will be very

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.040
bloody indeed by the series finale.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.080
Let's get the biggest one out of the way first.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.700
Cersei Lannister, the current holder of the
Iron Throne, will likely not survive the show.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.440
After all, the show loves to deliver on key
fan-anticipated moments, especially when it

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.680
involves revenge:

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.500
"When you brought me back to Winterfell, you
told me there's no justice in the world, not

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.580
unless we make it.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.640
Thank you for your many lessons, Lord Baelish."

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.540
There's more to the story than just offing
a villain, though.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.920
Cersei is now at odds with her brother Jaime,
setting up a situation in which he could be

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.340
the one who finally kills her.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.780
The Kingslayer Jaime Lannister could become
The Queenslayer, giving his sister and lover

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.840
some poetic justice along the way.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:58.210
And then, of course, there's that prophecy
Cersei received as a child which told her

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.059
a younger queen would take away all she held
dear.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:05.500
Cersei thought it would be Margaery Tyrell,
but it might actually be Daenerys Targaryen.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.960
Either way, she's surrounded by enemies going
into the final season.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.799
If a single human character is going to kill
Cersei Lannister, it seems quite likely that

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.680
her brother and lover Jaime will be the one
to swing the sword.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.399
Jaime's watched Cersei slowly unravel to the
point that her power may now threaten all

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.600
of humanity, and he may find the strength
in the final season to end her reign himself.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.360
Cersei is clever, though, and she still has
many resources at her command, including the

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.180
chemically altered enforcer that was Gregor
Clegane.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.600
Jaime may kill Cersei, but if he tries, she
will very likely end up being the death of

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.240
him as well.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:43.500
The last time we saw the mysterious Red Woman,
Melisandre told Varys that she was leaving

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.180
Westeros for Volantis.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.180
Despite her planned trip abroad, we've got
one very good reason to suspect that Melisandre

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:55.100
and Varys won't make it out alive: she's prophesied
it, and her magic powers means that her words

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.070
carry some serious narrative weight:

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.940
"I will return, dear spider.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.160
One last time.”

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.000
“My lady…”

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.600
“I have to die in this strange country.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.180
Just like you."

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.820
The real question is who will do the dubious
honor of killing them?

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:14.720
Melisandre is still on Arya's list, while
Varys has made a fair number of enemies in

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.400
his time.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.980
Fans are eagerly awaiting one specific moment
in the final season: for Sandor and Gregor

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:24.780
Clegane to finally duel it out to the death
after their twisted adventures.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:29.780
The season 7 finale only served to stoke this
fire, with the Hound seeming to promise that

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.000
the fight was coming:

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.140
"Doesn't matter.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.380
That’s not how it ends for you, brother.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:37.820
You know who's coming for you.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.380
You've always known."

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.500
The two brothers are clearly on opposing sides,
and while the real fight is with the army

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.660
of the dead, there could still be plenty of
time for a showdown for these two massive

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:50.840
men to kill each other.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.400
Game of Thrones loves to build someone up
only to tear them down.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.700
At the end of season 7, Grey Worm is one of
the characters who seems to be in a prime

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.580
position for just such a twist.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.980
He's found love with Missandei, he's found
a leader he can follow in Daenerys, and he

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.740
stands at the head of a great army.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.450
He's a leader, a warrior, and a trusted ally
who could prove pivotal in the fight against

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.000
the dead.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:16.540
He's also not going to let the Unsullied go
into battle without standing at the front

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:19.060
lines, and that makes him very vulnerable
indeed.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.920
Technically, Beric Dondarrion might already
be dead, since we last saw him standing on

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:27.150
the Wall just as the Night King brought a
section of it down.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.310
Still, it seems unlikely that the show would
kill him off-camera, so we'll assume he lives

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.280
to fight another day.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:37.060
With that in mind, Beric seems like a character
very likely to sacrifice himself in the final

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.959
season, and there's a key storytelling reason
for this.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.120
While beyond the Wall, he made a speech to
Jon about the importance of fighting against

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:44.620
death.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.400
"So what are you fighting for?"

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:48.100
"Life.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.360
Death is the enemy.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.540
The first enemy and the last."

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:58.069
That might just have been a prophecy for what's
coming for Beric, since shortly after this,

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:00.200
his personal resurrector died in battle.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.700
That leaves Beric with seemingly no way back
from his next death.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.400
A warrior's death that actually sticks would
be a fitting end.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.300
Few redemption arcs have come so far so far
as Theon Greyjoy's.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:16.880
He went from being the would-be lord of Winterfell
to being Ramsay Bolton's mutilated slave to

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.220
being a warrior for house Greyjoy once again.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:23.640
When we last saw him, he was sailing off to
try and rescue his sister Yara from the clutches

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.940
of his deceitful uncle.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:29.460
Theon is determined to right his past wrongs
by saving her and restoring their branch of

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:30.400
the family to power.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:35.030
What that means for the rest of the great
game is unclear, but for Theon himself it

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:38.080
means he's in a perfect position to pay the
ultimate price.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:42.530
A hero's sacrifice to save his sister and
the Iron Islands seems like the right way

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:43.020
to go.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:48.140
Few characters in Game of Thrones have suffered
so long in pursuit of a single thing as Jorah

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:48.980
Mormont.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:53.060
He's been to hell and back trying to win the
affection of Daenerys Targaryen.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.820
Last season it led him all the way to the
Citadel, where Samwell Tarly performed a painful

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.680
and dangerous procedure to rid him of his
greyscale.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:05.240
Now, cured of the disease that was supposed
to kill him, he has obeyed his queen and returned

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.880
to her side for what would seem to be the
last time.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:13.360
"When I take the seven kingdoms, I need you
by my side."

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:17.920
Jorah's love for and loyalty to Daenerys is
not in question, but his safety certainly

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:18.420
is.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.840
He has placed himself in deadly situations
countless times, and at this point he seems

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.980
destined to die in the fight to protect his
beloved khaleesi.

